.TH LAYERFAULT 1
.SH NAME
layerfault \- offline-first local AI model admission and behavioural security
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B layerfault
<command> [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Layerfault validates local AI model artifacts, packages, datasets, provenance, trust, runtime advisories and operator policy before admission or execution. On Linux, supported models can optionally be exercised inside a Bubblewrap sandbox for behavioural and runtime-side-effect evidence. Static scanning does not require an ML runtime.
.SH COMMANDS
scan, inspect, verify-file, scan-dir, fingerprint, verify-package, pipeline, verify, run, import, serve, trust, attest, audit, baseline, quarantine, policy, gc, doctor, capabilities, sources, explain, diff, compare, behaviour, compare-behaviour, review, models, drift, lineage, dataset, research, hub, platform, selftest, certify, advisories, evidence, version.
.SH SECURITY
Integrity, malformed-structure, scanner-error and invalid/revoked provenance failures are not operator-overridable. Active analysis is a hostile-code lab feature, not a proof of benign behaviour; run layerfault doctor and layerfault capabilities before active execution. See THREATS.md, SECURITY.md and docs/.
.SH COMPLETIONS
Shell completion files are shipped under completions/. Regenerate them and this page after CLI changes with scripts/build/cli-assets.sh.
